    "text": "The Chicago Cubs (1-2) send out right-hander Edward Cabrera for his Cubs debut on Monday as they open a three-game series at Wrigley Field with the Los Angeles Angels (2-2).CHICAGO, ILLINOIS - MARCH 29: Alex Bregman #3 of the Chicago Cubs celebrates a home run in the bottom of the fourth inning of a game against the Washi...How to Watch Angels vs CubsDate: Monday, March 30, 2026Time: 7:30 PM ETChannel: FanDuel Sports Network West, Marquee Sports NetworkStream: Fubo (TRY FOR FREE)Shota Imanaga surrendered a three-run homer in the top of the first, and Chicago never recovered while losing the decisive game of a three-game series with the Washington Nationals 6-3 on Sunday. Alex Bregman hit his first two home runs as a Cub, both solo shots, and Ian Happ also went deep. Imanaga struck out seven in five innings, but also gave up four runs on six hits.The Angels coughed up a 6-4 lead and took a 9-7 loss to the Houston Astros on Sunday that left them with a split of the four-game set in Houston. Zach Neto gave Los Angeles the lead with a two-run homer in the fourth after it had erased an early 4-0 deficit with four runs in the third, three coming on a bases-clearing double from Jorge Soler. Mike Trout opened the season by going 6-for-13 with two homers and seven walks in the series.Cabrera came to the Cubs in a trade from the Miami Marlins over the winter after putting up a 3.53 ERA and 1.228 WHIP in 26 starts and 137.2 innings with 150 strikeouts — all career highs. Ryan Johnson makes his first major-league start for Los Angeles on Monday night after making 14 relief appearances for the club last season. The rookie had a 7.36 ERA and 1.977 WHIP in 14.2 innings with 16 strikeouts before being optioned to High-A in early May 2025.Live stream Angels vs Cubs on Fubo: Start your free trial now!With Fubo, you can watch live television without cable on your phone, TV, or tablet. Fubo carries a wide array of sports and entertainment channels, including local sports packages and top national channels like ABC, FOX, CBS, ESPN, FS1, MTV, Comedy Central, and much more. The best part is you can try it out today for free.Regional restrictions may apply. If you purchase a product or register for an account through one of the links on our site, we may receive compensation.",
